[{:db/id "q-70955/selection/09f5f38b5d55249259c05c73c7fe9b92ebe291f6d916b92ac694d31a55134046" :answer/id #uuid "caefd944-7804-5d1e-a7b0-81a84c0998da" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,0,-\\sqrt{2})$ and $(6,0,-4)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70955/selection/9b4463455b5d037e72e92b3906d617aba93be31fa0ef82ce9595d5b1ad1cc59a" :answer/id #uuid "869f6a04-130a-54b6-a700-df11e8239ad6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,-4,0)$ and $(4,-2,-2\\sqrt{2})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70955/selection/e17cefbd556711f29790d8b9bd96c730f832dabfc5851e0965e9c31b05594410" :answer/id #uuid "a0503640-7340-574d-a246-8f1e935e67f5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(6,-4,0)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70955/selection/7f611d7d1cd203740fa2ebddd386a9ec033973f252ee437767ee70c706c6f70a" :answer/id #uuid "b2f03d6a-8a77-579c-98bb-7f3eb153cb64" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,-4,0)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70955/selection/9026c9e1a804f5e22f83605bb483dfb76d647ac5b00fc56de5d8feda678806b3" :answer/id #uuid "ddcf0723-4676-50b1-8b07-92ef849aa029" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-2,0,-4)$ and $(0,6,-4\\sqrt{2})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70955/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7c0fefb9-4da4-5721-ba08-d20540d3d103" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-70955/selection/9b4463455b5d037e72e92b3906d617aba93be31fa0ef82ce9595d5b1ad1cc59a" :answer-field/choices ["q-70955/selection/09f5f38b5d55249259c05c73c7fe9b92ebe291f6d916b92ac694d31a55134046" "q-70955/selection/9b4463455b5d037e72e92b3906d617aba93be31fa0ef82ce9595d5b1ad1cc59a" "q-70955/selection/e17cefbd556711f29790d8b9bd96c730f832dabfc5851e0965e9c31b05594410" "q-70955/selection/7f611d7d1cd203740fa2ebddd386a9ec033973f252ee437767ee70c706c6f70a" "q-70955/selection/9026c9e1a804f5e22f83605bb483dfb76d647ac5b00fc56de5d8feda678806b3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-70955" :question/id #uuid "a259cb2b-e950-5824-9397-ca2ca9ba3f74" :question/math-academy-id "q-70955" :question/problem "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the sphere $(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=16$ and the line \n${\\begin{aligned}x=2t+2 \\\\ y=2t-4\\,, \\\\ z=-2\\sqrt{2}t\\end{aligned}$ where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting the expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ from the parametric equation of the line into the equation of the sphere, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =16 \\\\ {((2t+2)-2)}^{2}+{(2t-4)}^{2}+{(-2\\sqrt{2}t)}^{2} & =16 \\\\ 4{t}^{2}+(4{t}^{2}-16t+16)+8{t}^{2} & =16 \\\\ 16{t}^{2}-16t+16 & =16 \\\\ 16{t}^{2}-16t & =0 \\\\ t(t-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $t=0$ and $t=1.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=0$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2(0)+2=2 \\\\ y=2(0)-4=-4 \\\\ z=-2\\sqrt{2}(0)=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $(2,-4,0).$\n\n- For $t=1$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2(1)+2=4 \\\\ y=2(1)-4=-2 \\\\ z=-2\\sqrt{2}(1)=-2\\sqrt{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $(4,-2,-2\\sqrt{2}).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(2,-4,0)$ and $(4,-2,-2\\sqrt{2}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-70955/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a426dc8c-2be0-5e83-93b6-54a634561aad"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70955"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-70954/selection/94ac6649c04765e1863b5b48b36a493d0e36b11d98edfaea4283ef8e69bce80c" :answer/id #uuid "7e1bf8bb-1644-5d7f-b2b9-5d4ffd450d5d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-2,-\\sqrt{2},2)$ and $(-1,0,\\sqrt{2})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70954/selection/c643b22b38440ee1a1652c2df5d27e63315fa15a0f0f1a5560c729a6cad64f82" :answer/id #uuid "aa0b41ac-8743-584d-aeda-360890155d50" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,\\sqrt{2},3)$ and $(1,2\\sqrt{2},2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70954/selection/1d16320a65316edac87c37804b2b35c8dc55713ee3e2ac04511873a023092b64" :answer/id #uuid "ef74b440-3cfb-5480-98bd-c857f8fbd7dc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,-\\sqrt{2},1)$ and $(0,0,2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70954/selection/f79822d71d90060300195d6c9ff71e961a5c22519e583dfe31f387e24750dfb6" :answer/id #uuid "1a5ff533-06dd-58df-80fb-3e67794d92d7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-1,-2\\sqrt{2},1)$ and $(0,0,2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70954/selection/55473653f8724a0d6bf294a2675497c3ad644a56a81c75971534eeed08449bcc" :answer/id #uuid "a223fe25-1337-5831-a52c-1da18146a174" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-\\sqrt{2},1,-1)$ and $(2,0,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70954/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "99060d62-00f9-59f5-9390-0e9fdf030737" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-70954/selection/1d16320a65316edac87c37804b2b35c8dc55713ee3e2ac04511873a023092b64" :answer-field/choices ["q-70954/selection/94ac6649c04765e1863b5b48b36a493d0e36b11d98edfaea4283ef8e69bce80c" "q-70954/selection/c643b22b38440ee1a1652c2df5d27e63315fa15a0f0f1a5560c729a6cad64f82" "q-70954/selection/1d16320a65316edac87c37804b2b35c8dc55713ee3e2ac04511873a023092b64" "q-70954/selection/f79822d71d90060300195d6c9ff71e961a5c22519e583dfe31f387e24750dfb6" "q-70954/selection/55473653f8724a0d6bf294a2675497c3ad644a56a81c75971534eeed08449bcc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-70954" :question/id #uuid "fce347c2-ad04-51e4-8225-7d5f64f3611a" :question/math-academy-id "q-70954" :question/problem "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=4$ and the line \n${\\begin{aligned}x=-t \\\\ y=\\sqrt{2}t, \\\\ z=t+2\\end{aligned}$ where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting the expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ from the parametric equation of the line into the equation of the sphere, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =4 \\\\ {(-t)}^{2}+{(\\sqrt{2}t)}^{2}+{(t+2)}^{2} & =4 \\\\ {t}^{2}+2{t}^{2}+({t}^{2}+4t+4) & =4 \\\\ 4{t}^{2}+4t+4 & =4 \\\\ 4{t}^{2}+4t & =0 \\\\ t(t+1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $t=-1$ and $t=0.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-(-1)=1 \\\\ y=\\sqrt{2}(-1)=-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ z=(-1)+2=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $(1,-\\sqrt{2},1).$\n\n- For $t=0$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=(0)=0 \\\\ y=\\sqrt{2}(0)=0 \\\\ z=(0)+2=2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $(0,0,2).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(1,-\\sqrt{2},1)$ and $(0,0,2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-70954/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a426dc8c-2be0-5e83-93b6-54a634561aad"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70954"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71950/selection/736e1498a18b9cf9988ff15bd24a79587c54573b7bbac788d0934d9d858f0888" :answer/id #uuid "e2ff7b9a-b9d4-5d8f-bf27-11032a09c613" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(5,0,0)$ and $(3,2,-2\\sqrt{3})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71950/selection/f49b60a593069d54e6bc70ebf86daef939996fbc503aff2b04c60b1715dfa938" :answer/id #uuid "4fafa0ed-b7c6-55e0-9219-fa8c11a890c7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(5,0,0)$ and $(1,-1,\\sqrt{3})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71950/selection/8dc813f8527dd1bbcb4c993f2cb1177f673b17f5091d06615a7dea02df707b79" :answer/id #uuid "8651e21b-2146-5275-a8a0-09ae0af1cb15" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,-1,\\sqrt{3})$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71950/selection/145fc891f9319b07c554cfda90579f26f05ce19355e34dc5fc1cc64e1d1b6e84" :answer/id #uuid "e2b9d2bf-311c-5945-9bb5-7f96b7ddbbc6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(3,2,-2\\sqrt{3})$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71950/selection/016ca7286e30c27967aeacdd36cf51baf2f791679b1bcb4e8f3e72330bfc4793" :answer/id #uuid "deb388bc-bc3b-5903-aa45-ff366b83119b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(5,0,0)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71950/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a0d6b296-3874-50f4-9cde-64aee7e50398" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71950/selection/736e1498a18b9cf9988ff15bd24a79587c54573b7bbac788d0934d9d858f0888" :answer-field/choices ["q-71950/selection/736e1498a18b9cf9988ff15bd24a79587c54573b7bbac788d0934d9d858f0888" "q-71950/selection/f49b60a593069d54e6bc70ebf86daef939996fbc503aff2b04c60b1715dfa938" "q-71950/selection/8dc813f8527dd1bbcb4c993f2cb1177f673b17f5091d06615a7dea02df707b79" "q-71950/selection/145fc891f9319b07c554cfda90579f26f05ce19355e34dc5fc1cc64e1d1b6e84" "q-71950/selection/016ca7286e30c27967aeacdd36cf51baf2f791679b1bcb4e8f3e72330bfc4793"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71950" :question/id #uuid "a1773b77-a320-5735-8636-86d18d67fe9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-71950" :question/problem "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=25$ and the line \n${\\begin{aligned}x=2t+5 \\\\ y=-2t, \\\\ z=2\\sqrt{3}t\\end{aligned}$ where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting the expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ from the parametric equation of the line into the equation of the sphere, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =25 \\\\ (2t+5)^{2}+(-2t)^{2}+(2\\sqrt{3}t)^{2} & =25 \\\\ (4{t}^{2}+20t+25)+4{t}^{2}+12{t}^{2} & =25 \\\\ 20{t}^{2}+20t+25 & =25 \\\\ 20{t}^{2}+20t & =0 \\\\ 20t(t+1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $t=0$ and $t=-1.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=0$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2(0)+5=5 \\\\ y=-2(0)=0 \\\\ z=2\\sqrt{3}(0)=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $(5,0,0).$\n\n- For $t=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2(-1)+5=3 \\\\ y=-2(-1)=2 \\\\ z=2\\sqrt{3}(-1)=-2\\sqrt{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $(3,2,-2\\sqrt{3}).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(5,0,0)$ and $(3,2,-2\\sqrt{3}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-71950/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a426dc8c-2be0-5e83-93b6-54a634561aad"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71950"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71131/selection/fad419202faa5b95201b42b0597088e05cc0b9345926263270d568d2fc1673ec" :answer/id #uuid "4983bb6e-2241-5232-9449-cb87813a2b25" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,0,0)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71131/selection/60d58cef990e6ce611c8db3af38c40c33841e808e4aa4367561a173d0919c4cd" :answer/id #uuid "e3eb340a-4b98-5b03-ae9e-d49e5c25c482" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(\\frac{5}{9},-\\frac{4}{9},\\frac{4}{9})$ and $(2,1,-1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71131/selection/8768e704243456bb031773a7f64c380f63e61d35850fc40651b454c46fe3198c" :answer/id #uuid "d9064b4b-933c-5384-be54-fbe8ee10f78d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(\\frac{5}{9},-\\frac{4}{9},\\frac{4}{9})$ and $(1,0,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71131/selection/03abb4a26038b5dc70660660ae1e243fb57b9a2a310bcbf07e098e1117817531" :answer/id #uuid "83f83ac5-968e-551d-9e75-4621287de4ee" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(\\frac{5}{9},-\\frac{4}{9},\\frac{4}{9})$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71131/selection/a80fbb8a917ab64bd2c66ae423b17f422209c4c8c734bfd5e8a8de8ed324eced" :answer/id #uuid "2695182b-1ccb-5776-a4cf-4f39d2d57db5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,1,-1)$ and $(1,0,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71131/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4b0d241e-6fef-5d83-b82e-c846f17648a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71131/selection/8768e704243456bb031773a7f64c380f63e61d35850fc40651b454c46fe3198c" :answer-field/choices ["q-71131/selection/fad419202faa5b95201b42b0597088e05cc0b9345926263270d568d2fc1673ec" "q-71131/selection/60d58cef990e6ce611c8db3af38c40c33841e808e4aa4367561a173d0919c4cd" "q-71131/selection/8768e704243456bb031773a7f64c380f63e61d35850fc40651b454c46fe3198c" "q-71131/selection/03abb4a26038b5dc70660660ae1e243fb57b9a2a310bcbf07e098e1117817531" "q-71131/selection/a80fbb8a917ab64bd2c66ae423b17f422209c4c8c734bfd5e8a8de8ed324eced"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71131" :question/id #uuid "b828b568-be9f-5fe6-8a19-4f466a780e15" :question/math-academy-id "q-71131" :question/problem "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the ellipsoid ${x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2}=1$ and the line \n${\\begin{aligned}x=1+t \\\\ y=t, \\\\ z=-t\\end{aligned}$ where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting the expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ from the parametric equation of the line into the equation of the ellipsoid, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}+6{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =2 \\\\ 2(1+t)^{2}+6(t)^{2}+(-t)^{2} & =2 \\\\ 2(1+2t+{t}^{2})+6{t}^{2}+{t}^{2} & =2 \\\\ 2+4t+2{t}^{2}+6{t}^{2}+{t}^{2} & =2 \\\\ 9{t}^{2}+4t & =0 \\\\ t(9t+4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $t=-\\frac{4}{9}$ and $t=0.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=-\\frac{4}{9}$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+(-\\frac{4}{9})=\\frac{5}{9} \\\\ y=-\\frac{4}{9} \\\\ z=-(-\\frac{4}{9})=\\frac{4}{9},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $(\\frac{5}{9},-\\frac{4}{9},\\frac{4}{9}).$\n\n- For $t=0$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+0=1 \\\\ y=0 \\\\ z=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $(1,0,0).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(\\frac{5}{9},-\\frac{4}{9},\\frac{4}{9})$ and $(1,0,0).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-71131/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a426dc8c-2be0-5e83-93b6-54a634561aad"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71131"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-70568"] :question/problem "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the ellipsoid $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}=1$ and the line \n${\\begin{aligned}x=t \\\\ y=2t, \\\\ z=t\\end{aligned}$ where $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting the expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ from the parametric equation of the line into the equation of the ellipsoid, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4} & =1 \\\\ 8{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2} & =16 \\\\ 8(t)^{2}+(2t)^{2}+4(t)^{2} & =16 \\\\ 8{t}^{2}+4{t}^{2}+4{t}^{2} & =16 \\\\ 16{t}^{2} & =16 \\\\ {t}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $t=-1$ and $t=1.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=(-1)=-1 \\\\ y=2(-1)=-2 \\\\ z=(-1)=-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $(-1,-2,-1).$\n\n- For $t=1$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=(1)=1 \\\\ y=2(1)=2 \\\\ z=(1)=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $(1,2,1).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(-1,-2,-1)$ and $(1,2,1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-94785/selection/ae75935059fea7c013a3e888252e2e9d64e083afbc58587147c6e9d49ec4cbc9" :answer/id #uuid "c820b5a1-ad62-5fc7-a8a8-bf4cd22bd8d6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(6,1,6)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94785/selection/666bacef2fa0ca7528cdba12280de92e9138fad861c35f26462ea90cc80045d2" :answer/id #uuid "2bf731e3-69c4-534f-aeee-e731635f07cf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(3,0,3)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94785/selection/855464a65e1c92b98fc036fa55ef5fa7961383b6343dfd8f9807b4e24e183e87" :answer/id #uuid "1f240cb8-72c4-5baf-8a17-51b59f157fe9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-3,-2,-3)$  and $(0,-1,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94785/selection/96ca8f7e8f4265087dee73603146546246d6ea3861c00ced8db0d3f88c9de071" :answer/id #uuid "26b26f6e-609a-5e13-8038-50053beecdd5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(0,-1,0)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94785/selection/269b6198329155b2d1f896421402227395e23f550b977386cebeea4481bb6df4" :answer/id #uuid "71e0555e-9121-5bcd-8612-c3317fc0555e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-6,-3,-6)$ and $(3,0,3)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94785/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "197a9ca9-fe4b-5369-8cf1-14f9f99a8d49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94785/selection/666bacef2fa0ca7528cdba12280de92e9138fad861c35f26462ea90cc80045d2" :answer-field/choices ["q-94785/selection/ae75935059fea7c013a3e888252e2e9d64e083afbc58587147c6e9d49ec4cbc9" "q-94785/selection/666bacef2fa0ca7528cdba12280de92e9138fad861c35f26462ea90cc80045d2" "q-94785/selection/855464a65e1c92b98fc036fa55ef5fa7961383b6343dfd8f9807b4e24e183e87" "q-94785/selection/96ca8f7e8f4265087dee73603146546246d6ea3861c00ced8db0d3f88c9de071" "q-94785/selection/269b6198329155b2d1f896421402227395e23f550b977386cebeea4481bb6df4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94785" :question/id #uuid "c7a9912a-e8fa-5a3a-bbb8-69d846d6c8b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-94785" :question/problem "Find the point of the intersection of the elliptic cone $2{x}^{2}+5{y}^{2}=2{z}^{2}$ and the line $\\frac{x}{3}=y+1=\\frac{z}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation of our line in the parametric form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{3}=y+1=\\frac{z}{3}=t\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}x=3t \\\\ y=t-1 \\\\ z=3t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSubstituting the above expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+5{y}^{2} & =2{z}^{2} \\\\ 2(3t)^{2}+5(t-1)^{2} & =2(3t)^{2} \\\\ 5(t-1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ (t-1)^{2} & =0 \\\\ t-1 & =0 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute our solution back into the equations of the line. For $t=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3(1)=3 \\\\ y=1-1=0 \\\\ z=3(1)=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is $(3,0,3).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94785/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5329867-1956-5f36-8614-26d483c36efe"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94785"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71138/selection/ea583dd8941b7dc605a948d63ff9ad12aa3b1477f376c70dd39c15f44734e4b3" :answer/id #uuid "75e844cd-366f-5828-b211-47a8d2eb883f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2})$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71138/selection/db9bdd72fe4fac6b5ce72edb6765606372dbcdfec86ad1a692a6c9be73e2c8fc" :answer/id #uuid "77612699-32f2-5449-9939-76eb5987037d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(3,-1,1)$ and $(-3,1,-1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71138/selection/5f78486e0a0ed2fccd0bc0b4b70f06b00199c7b6e4fa6e4738eb0502287747a9" :answer/id #uuid "aa233271-2042-5fd2-a81b-73dbab228206" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(\\frac{3}{2},-\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{1}{2})$ and $(\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71138/selection/5d6c8aba0129e5cca9ab7397f106bb68cb2da4cbd8dee771d737d327d8ac49ed" :answer/id #uuid "76b81460-e402-5210-95c3-1fdf333ad999" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(3,1,1)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71138/selection/253eab615f2d021d707cd2eb1e5b67e03969305da3feb1478a5f9e6f863fb86e" :answer/id #uuid "5fe4dbfd-9c66-5922-bd0f-a4bac460d0a7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-3,-1,-1)$ and $(3,1,1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71138/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "99edd550-4875-594e-a8e0-4fcb00d61805" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71138/selection/253eab615f2d021d707cd2eb1e5b67e03969305da3feb1478a5f9e6f863fb86e" :answer-field/choices ["q-71138/selection/ea583dd8941b7dc605a948d63ff9ad12aa3b1477f376c70dd39c15f44734e4b3" "q-71138/selection/db9bdd72fe4fac6b5ce72edb6765606372dbcdfec86ad1a692a6c9be73e2c8fc" "q-71138/selection/5f78486e0a0ed2fccd0bc0b4b70f06b00199c7b6e4fa6e4738eb0502287747a9" "q-71138/selection/5d6c8aba0129e5cca9ab7397f106bb68cb2da4cbd8dee771d737d327d8ac49ed" "q-71138/selection/253eab615f2d021d707cd2eb1e5b67e03969305da3feb1478a5f9e6f863fb86e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71138" :question/id #uuid "36de663b-cc76-5deb-ab88-1e5621d5cc58" :question/math-academy-id "q-71138" :question/problem "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the ellipsoid $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{15}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{5}=1$ and the line $\\frac{x}{6}=\\frac{y}{2}=\\frac{z}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation of our line in parametric form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{6}=\\frac{y}{2}=\\frac{z}{2}=t\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}x=6t \\\\ y=2t \\\\ z=2t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSubstituting the above expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ into the equation of the ellipsoid, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{15}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{5} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}+3{z}^{2} & =15 \\\\ (6t)^{2}+3(2t)^{2}+3(2t)^{2} & =15 \\\\ 36{t}^{2}+12{t}^{2}+12{t}^{2} & =15 \\\\ 60{t}^{2} & =15 \\\\ {t}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $t=-\\frac{1}{2}$ and $t=\\frac{1}{2}.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=-\\frac{1}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=6(-\\frac{1}{2})=-3 \\\\ y=2(-\\frac{1}{2})=-1 \\\\ z=2(-\\frac{1}{2})=-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $(-3,-1,-1).$\n\n- For $t=\\frac{1}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=6(\\frac{1}{2})=3 \\\\ y=2(\\frac{1}{2})=1 \\\\ z=2(\\frac{1}{2})=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $(3,1,1).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(-3,-1,-1)$ and $(3,1,1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71138/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5329867-1956-5f36-8614-26d483c36efe"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71138"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71955/selection/d59d1558e2df2d8bd2d27a76388dd875d94c44c1410836cac87cc800352f685d" :answer/id #uuid "68a8d125-6ecc-5653-ab88-0c1553e911f7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(3,-7,0)$ and $(-1,-9,-2\\sqrt{2})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71955/selection/fe5eaeea0a33c6628597d2133c4199bddb856db42027c1ae8efe0df364383bc0" :answer/id #uuid "16b61138-1bc3-5c07-8c0f-f7a1ebaaf864" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(3,-7,0)$ and $(7,-5,\\sqrt{2})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71955/selection/30bc6c06baaae5f171d4e455505de6be56d111d59cca88ef55afaa13ac7babe0" :answer/id #uuid "68539c8b-54c2-5a9b-9397-e2d755087baa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(3,-7,0)$ and $(7,5,2\\sqrt{2})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71955/selection/0827fa1989e007fa5a09d69320e24dd0f752cdbec749ae9ecc30e9cc3943a42d" :answer/id #uuid "fe2ac92f-7663-5c29-bc12-7ae65c3e64bb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(3,-7,0)$ and $(-1,9,2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71955/selection/51f2df22abee1ba2a947ec3b92764486df26052141efb6fd2f570fcac321a655" :answer/id #uuid "2d76cb29-3a9a-5c0d-9f82-e663d47b84a6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(3,-7,0)$ and $(7,-5,2\\sqrt{2})$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71955/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9ac42f67-29bb-5bda-bdc6-8948c689fbf6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71955/selection/51f2df22abee1ba2a947ec3b92764486df26052141efb6fd2f570fcac321a655" :answer-field/choices ["q-71955/selection/d59d1558e2df2d8bd2d27a76388dd875d94c44c1410836cac87cc800352f685d" "q-71955/selection/fe5eaeea0a33c6628597d2133c4199bddb856db42027c1ae8efe0df364383bc0" "q-71955/selection/30bc6c06baaae5f171d4e455505de6be56d111d59cca88ef55afaa13ac7babe0" "q-71955/selection/0827fa1989e007fa5a09d69320e24dd0f752cdbec749ae9ecc30e9cc3943a42d" "q-71955/selection/51f2df22abee1ba2a947ec3b92764486df26052141efb6fd2f570fcac321a655"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71955" :question/id #uuid "e2185543-6678-579f-aacb-46fdcc834d66" :question/math-academy-id "q-71955" :question/problem "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the sphere $(x-3)^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=49$ and the line $\\frac{x-3}{2}=y+7=\\frac{z}{\\sqrt{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation of our line in parametric form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{2}=\\frac{y+7}{1}=\\frac{z}{\\sqrt{2}}=t\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}x=2t+3 \\\\ y=t-7 \\\\ z=\\sqrt{2}t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSubstituting the above expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ into the equation of the sphere, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-3)^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =49 \\\\ ((2t+3)-3)^{2}+(t-7)^{2}+(\\sqrt{2}t)^{2} & =49 \\\\ (2t)^{2}+(t-7)^{2}+(\\sqrt{2}t)^{2} & =49 \\\\ 4{t}^{2}+({t}^{2}-14t+49)+2{t}^{2} & =49 \\\\ 7{t}^{2}-14t+49 & =49 \\\\ 7{t}^{2}-14t & =0 \\\\ 7t(t-2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $t=0$ and $t=2.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=0$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2(0)+3=3 \\\\ y=(0)-7=-7 \\\\ z=\\sqrt{2}(0)=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $(3,-7,0).$\n\n- For $t=2$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2(2)+3=7 \\\\ y=(2)-7=-5 \\\\ z=\\sqrt{2}(2)=2\\sqrt{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $(7,-5,2\\sqrt{2}).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(3,-7,0)$ and $(7,-5,2\\sqrt{2}).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71955/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5329867-1956-5f36-8614-26d483c36efe"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71955"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-70961/selection/1a8f9b77315d63ca87641bedb663b67dc049cf24af47ce287c330784127f3c3f" :answer/id #uuid "1063182f-b4a6-5b70-875b-48fc48e0330d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,-6,-11)$ and $(4,0,-9)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70961/selection/7ba006931c5f0f1108096ba17db54d9f288183c4af32444706c8e5ef01f5ccac" :answer/id #uuid "0628bfe2-484e-5bcc-b5b3-c91c2626010d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(6,-2,-11)$ and $(0,4,-9)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70961/selection/e9950376e517f7f6eafe8a41c4ae3e2d0eb46b33d7c5e57bbe356f97d8d38bad" :answer/id #uuid "80983f67-27fd-56d4-b2e5-e333adfd645b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,-6,-2)$ and $(9,0,-4)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70961/selection/065345011f5f37d4e296d98cafb35532942cef8ad53190f3be610dad60a90ea5" :answer/id #uuid "902e4f94-cd05-5409-a930-f4a27cb901fb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,6,-1)$ and $(-9,0,4)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70961/selection/175a23d371b51dc262e1e1c11f8c177f4c3b36eb392f96ef2374776181a37226" :answer/id #uuid "85f2f45b-6672-5c30-a833-2d8b5f8d1a57" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,-11,-6)$ and $(4,9,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-70961/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "189db109-5bd5-576f-8245-aba84dda5880" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-70961/selection/1a8f9b77315d63ca87641bedb663b67dc049cf24af47ce287c330784127f3c3f" :answer-field/choices ["q-70961/selection/1a8f9b77315d63ca87641bedb663b67dc049cf24af47ce287c330784127f3c3f" "q-70961/selection/7ba006931c5f0f1108096ba17db54d9f288183c4af32444706c8e5ef01f5ccac" "q-70961/selection/e9950376e517f7f6eafe8a41c4ae3e2d0eb46b33d7c5e57bbe356f97d8d38bad" "q-70961/selection/065345011f5f37d4e296d98cafb35532942cef8ad53190f3be610dad60a90ea5" "q-70961/selection/175a23d371b51dc262e1e1c11f8c177f4c3b36eb392f96ef2374776181a37226"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-70961" :question/id #uuid "6a7886ea-95b6-5ef1-bc81-bad1e923f2d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-70961" :question/problem "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the sphere $(x-2)^{2}+(y+6)^{2}+{z}^{2}=121$ and the line $\\frac{x-2}{2}=\\frac{y+6}{6}=\\frac{z+11}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation of our line in parametric form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-2}{2}=\\frac{y+6}{6}=\\frac{z+11}{2}=t\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}x=2t+2 \\\\ y=6t-6 \\\\ z=2t-11,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSubstituting the above expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ into the equation of the sphere, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+(y+6)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =121 \\\\ ((2t+2)-2)^{2}+((6t-6)+6)^{2}+(2t-11)^{2} & =121 \\\\ (2t)^{2}+(6t)^{2}+(2t-11)^{2} & =121 \\\\ 4{t}^{2}+36{t}^{2}+(4{t}^{2}-44t+121) & =121 \\\\ 44{t}^{2}-44t+121 & =121 \\\\ 44{t}^{2}-44t & =0 \\\\ t(t-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $t=0$ and $t=1.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=0$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2(0)+2=2 \\\\ y=6(0)-6=-6 \\\\ z=2(0)-11=-11,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $(2,-6,-11).$\n\n- For $t=1$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2(1)+2=4 \\\\ y=6(1)-6=0 \\\\ z=2(1)-11=-9,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $(4,0,-9).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(2,-6,-11)$ and $(4,0,-9).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-70961/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5329867-1956-5f36-8614-26d483c36efe"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-70961"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94784/selection/a5b67770bc022193437161af8c3f4524664f2975d39fbdc95075fc12ee02f41e" :answer/id #uuid "e517a2b6-ffb3-59df-85a0-94ffce2ea96e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(2,2,-4)$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94784/selection/4002285fda69b9768e71728b917a060e9607a879d359df97a363b6337b9087e9" :answer/id #uuid "0c54e040-0ada-51b6-8a72-999b584c38a1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-1,-1,-10)$  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94784/selection/44d420420b1cd3d29372ff75ae5b8d32876c43c04eb180d6c8f96f94983b579e" :answer/id #uuid "878fa694-127c-5301-92f2-836789620487" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(3,3,-2)$  and $(-1,-1,-10)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94784/selection/9375204d3d06be9c1f2ae1e6d29dd9906dc5c3eaecc14deea906fe830c6066c7" :answer/id #uuid "24780450-ff62-53b1-ae6c-ca08f78d4459" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,1,-6)$  and $(2,2,-4)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94784/selection/85d555f9c35bc4387482f2e57254dada00e728fa7614e468c262d52bdb7aa205" :answer/id #uuid "20780e38-5285-5b15-a089-2423b26b1f13" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-2,-2,-12)$   only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94784/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7e5df432-e6e8-5c64-b25f-6e669ab6bb3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94784/selection/a5b67770bc022193437161af8c3f4524664f2975d39fbdc95075fc12ee02f41e" :answer-field/choices ["q-94784/selection/a5b67770bc022193437161af8c3f4524664f2975d39fbdc95075fc12ee02f41e" "q-94784/selection/4002285fda69b9768e71728b917a060e9607a879d359df97a363b6337b9087e9" "q-94784/selection/44d420420b1cd3d29372ff75ae5b8d32876c43c04eb180d6c8f96f94983b579e" "q-94784/selection/9375204d3d06be9c1f2ae1e6d29dd9906dc5c3eaecc14deea906fe830c6066c7" "q-94784/selection/85d555f9c35bc4387482f2e57254dada00e728fa7614e468c262d52bdb7aa205"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94784" :question/id #uuid "3dc5f127-8068-54c4-b54b-8ddcd406e234" :question/math-academy-id "q-94784" :question/problem "Find the point of the intersection of the elliptic cone $2{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}={z}^{2}$ and the line $x=y=\\frac{z+8}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation of our line in parametric form:\n\n$$\nx=y=\\frac{z+8}{2}=t\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}x=t \\\\ y=t \\\\ z=2t-8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSubstituting the above expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ 2{t}^{2}+2{t}^{2} & =(2t-8)^{2} \\\\ 4{t}^{2} & =4{t}^{2}-32t+64 \\\\ 32t & =64 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute our solution back into the equations of the line. For $t=2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2 \\\\ y=2 \\\\ z=2(2)-8=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection is $(2,2,-4).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94784/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b5329867-1956-5f36-8614-26d483c36efe"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94784"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73866/selection/a6c90435c259a0a1a2fbbc4926cd3f5d871e70bfa03e1026bdfbb588dd7aca94" :answer/id #uuid "66594093-3fff-546c-92b5-7a2493f8a697" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,0)$ in the $xz$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73866/selection/2ff5a13cf86b4c5f7a2e954d6d62be99a14d2eacec96696d84c33f1c5330ad94" :answer/id #uuid "04fc3548-12a9-571b-9dd8-5ce4069c9ebc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,-2)$ in the $xz$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73866/selection/63de505a2edd7355d46fd8a34d5c3f3c54d344be6d8f5f4ac493c57b555a6267" :answer/id #uuid "530613f5-a721-58c6-b989-a74c9746bc50" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(1,-5)$ in the $xz$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73866/selection/38e4b840ac179249093a29a3642c137aa12796d0ee9e24c0b9165d8da194765e" :answer/id #uuid "c076f2c1-2c22-5ab8-b69c-93de4945e632" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-1,5)$ in the $xz$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73866/selection/cb8046d4e46674cc28e159904819635904dd809d861e0602643a046a03127a1d" :answer/id #uuid "179f9e7c-53eb-56e1-8d03-64d4037dcba7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-1,2)$ in the $xz$-plane" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73866/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e441e264-9702-5335-8ef0-7b56770206da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73866/selection/2ff5a13cf86b4c5f7a2e954d6d62be99a14d2eacec96696d84c33f1c5330ad94" :answer-field/choices ["q-73866/selection/a6c90435c259a0a1a2fbbc4926cd3f5d871e70bfa03e1026bdfbb588dd7aca94" "q-73866/selection/2ff5a13cf86b4c5f7a2e954d6d62be99a14d2eacec96696d84c33f1c5330ad94" "q-73866/selection/63de505a2edd7355d46fd8a34d5c3f3c54d344be6d8f5f4ac493c57b555a6267" "q-73866/selection/38e4b840ac179249093a29a3642c137aa12796d0ee9e24c0b9165d8da194765e" "q-73866/selection/cb8046d4e46674cc28e159904819635904dd809d861e0602643a046a03127a1d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73866" :question/id #uuid "cc9a60c0-9b27-537d-8f7e-b89ae32845f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-73866" :question/problem "For the elliptic paraboloid $\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}=z+5$, the section in the plane $\\sqrt{3}x-2y=2\\sqrt{3}$ is a parabola. \nFind the vertex of the projection of this parabola onto $xz$-plane." :question/worked-solution "Since we want to find the projection onto the $xz$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $y.$ First, we solve for $y$ in the equation of the plane, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3}x-2y=2\\sqrt{3}\\,⟹\\,y=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}(x-2)}{2}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $y$ into the equation of the paraboloid, we obtain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{4}+{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}(x-2)}{2})}^{2} & =z+5 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{3(x-2)^{2}}{4} & =z+5 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}+4x+4}{4}+\\frac{3{x}^{2}-12x+12}{4} & =z+5 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}-8x+16}{4} & =z+5 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+4 & =z+5 \\\\ z & ={x}^{2}-2x-1 \\\\ z & =({x}^{2}-2x+1)-2 \\\\ z & ={(x-1)}^{2}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the vertex of the projection onto $xz$-plane is $(1,-2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73866/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "58427e6a-8e77-5c01-a578-a7dc4b8f8812"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73866"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71027/selection/a387f3a22fa97d4857d31b42902837e28ddd2bc5d75ca6596d48914c6e48c6d0" :answer/id #uuid "d990f855-5feb-5d7d-88e3-1c9d24422320" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{6}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71027/selection/59b9138bd1be28864f25608c5c133149fc9660a21085e6fd0636caff7792ae96" :answer/id #uuid "7a77e354-5bc4-5452-8abe-355406ea2a72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{3}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71027/selection/49e029a7bd9f9b575fb7fb351c6d052c9aafff3170a3ee5aee1600d2f4cd204b" :answer/id #uuid "c84062d7-1f62-5473-8c4b-df1d85173d6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{6}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71027/selection/dcc1540897efe7dcba5d99e6ff6a1a3dd1e9b989b4411c495596c493a6dbb89a" :answer/id #uuid "4f7516a4-1e19-5046-81f5-44077f414d6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71027/selection/a86fcf1ef952b97cffca2b663342ef3ddebeb28382d262a5568b156fe3a83a55" :answer/id #uuid "c08c7ca4-1e4d-5e7c-97b6-c87fcf7dff25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{12}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{6}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71027/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6ae41450-b4dc-5864-b690-150aab3f2521" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71027/selection/59b9138bd1be28864f25608c5c133149fc9660a21085e6fd0636caff7792ae96" :answer-field/choices ["q-71027/selection/a387f3a22fa97d4857d31b42902837e28ddd2bc5d75ca6596d48914c6e48c6d0" "q-71027/selection/59b9138bd1be28864f25608c5c133149fc9660a21085e6fd0636caff7792ae96" "q-71027/selection/49e029a7bd9f9b575fb7fb351c6d052c9aafff3170a3ee5aee1600d2f4cd204b" "q-71027/selection/dcc1540897efe7dcba5d99e6ff6a1a3dd1e9b989b4411c495596c493a6dbb89a" "q-71027/selection/a86fcf1ef952b97cffca2b663342ef3ddebeb28382d262a5568b156fe3a83a55"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71027" :question/id #uuid "2b71c9ae-ee46-5232-a1a3-d49ef79f550d" :question/math-academy-id "q-71027" :question/problem "Find the projection of the intersection between the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=24$ and the plane $z+y=6$ onto the $xy$-plane." :question/worked-solution "Since we want to find the projection onto the $xy$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $z.$ First, we solve for $z$ in the equation of the plane, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z+y & =6\\,⟹\\,z=6-y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $z$ into the equation of the sphere, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2} & =24 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+(6-y)^{2} & =24 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+(36-12y+{y}^{2}) & =24 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-12y+36 & =24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by completing the square for the variable $y$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-12y+36 & =24 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}-12{y}^{2}+18 & =6 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2({y}^{2}-6{y}^{2}+9) & =6 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2(y-3)^{2} & =6 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{3} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the projection of the intersection is the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{3}=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-71027/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "58427e6a-8e77-5c01-a578-a7dc4b8f8812"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71027"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71963/selection/aa3bdde15c73dda02623808356522f85887a373f525032323aece1d66070c7b5" :answer/id #uuid "403b3250-881e-5c28-94d8-d6a5afa98b35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{3}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71963/selection/1ffb8098e30bf43fc4675c09226724de1c261bd0313a749e7c2ece11f39c0a36" :answer/id #uuid "57d54833-1be4-56e5-b6f8-c5e2c02e5bf2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{3}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71963/selection/49d6358b9d118afc782097e1b50a26b548442123ad662bf23b231fc8cd21ad24" :answer/id #uuid "b494e1e9-2d6b-57d8-8604-07a91f4cdbe4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71963/selection/3b9f2fd2d499ef54dd2831277b7fb85e9d9cc39a29bc1012cda4d92f26e60d55" :answer/id #uuid "be8fe5b4-95cd-5f71-86d3-eb6ff23cb2d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{2}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71963/selection/6dcdc5242220b9ecbbd470a12359b668cb82debaca256f8c2521ed92945632eb" :answer/id #uuid "bfbb619e-5b9c-552b-bd64-3ba350f88aca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{3}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71963/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "467a5a73-ed31-5eb7-b3fe-c985988fcb0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71963/selection/aa3bdde15c73dda02623808356522f85887a373f525032323aece1d66070c7b5" :answer-field/choices ["q-71963/selection/aa3bdde15c73dda02623808356522f85887a373f525032323aece1d66070c7b5" "q-71963/selection/1ffb8098e30bf43fc4675c09226724de1c261bd0313a749e7c2ece11f39c0a36" "q-71963/selection/49d6358b9d118afc782097e1b50a26b548442123ad662bf23b231fc8cd21ad24" "q-71963/selection/3b9f2fd2d499ef54dd2831277b7fb85e9d9cc39a29bc1012cda4d92f26e60d55" "q-71963/selection/6dcdc5242220b9ecbbd470a12359b668cb82debaca256f8c2521ed92945632eb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71963" :question/id #uuid "519971ff-8426-53f7-a046-fcb25af4692b" :question/math-academy-id "q-71963" :question/problem "Find the projection of the intersection between the sphere ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=8$ and the plane $z-y=2$ onto the $xz$-plane." :question/worked-solution "Since we want to find the projection onto the $xz$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $y.$ First, we solve for $y$ in the equation of the plane, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-y & =2\\,⟹\\,y=z-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $y$ into the equation of the sphere, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+(z-2)^{2}+{z}^{2} & =8 \\\\ {x}^{2}+({z}^{2}-4z+4)+{z}^{2} & =8 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2{z}^{2}-4z+4 & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by completing the square for the variable $z$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+2{z}^{2}-4z+4 & =8 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2{z}^{2}-4z+2 & =6 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2({z}^{2}-2z+1) & =6 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2(z-1)^{2} & =6 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{3} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the projection of the intersection is the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{(z-1)^{2}}{3}=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71963/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "58427e6a-8e77-5c01-a578-a7dc4b8f8812"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71963"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71975/selection/85240ac915c3d224da3c080e8ceda14d2a7cdbb13bce7cfc5788b73eb020b668" :answer/id #uuid "99f52092-9b2c-5054-bfda-26e2bf675d07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{8}=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71975/selection/44dc8517f78c03bd2948081f118a56b017bb6de750d4e272935a4ee8762169ac" :answer/id #uuid "0771881b-8d2f-56e9-93ff-c616808b0312" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{8}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71975/selection/c7215761c7ec982cdc50c97b091b18bfd266eb30995692698d75a0f7416fb9d3" :answer/id #uuid "1b078336-640b-5302-81c6-dcb6913830a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{8}=-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71975/selection/800bd49e2c542f739e1d7e6e25ac8fd754d6df306ab550460ab7744dfdb7095b" :answer/id #uuid "b57fc7c5-897c-53cf-bc65-40e25ebccc52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{8}=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71975/selection/b275d36a52703c6f9915aaaea03cb3d229704e5cdda18d6a027dd66932add5b7" :answer/id #uuid "f7c4166f-2e64-55b9-bc1b-2d89406787f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71975/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ce4a3a0-dc1f-55bd-93fa-8edffacc7e00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71975/selection/44dc8517f78c03bd2948081f118a56b017bb6de750d4e272935a4ee8762169ac" :answer-field/choices ["q-71975/selection/85240ac915c3d224da3c080e8ceda14d2a7cdbb13bce7cfc5788b73eb020b668" "q-71975/selection/44dc8517f78c03bd2948081f118a56b017bb6de750d4e272935a4ee8762169ac" "q-71975/selection/c7215761c7ec982cdc50c97b091b18bfd266eb30995692698d75a0f7416fb9d3" "q-71975/selection/800bd49e2c542f739e1d7e6e25ac8fd754d6df306ab550460ab7744dfdb7095b" "q-71975/selection/b275d36a52703c6f9915aaaea03cb3d229704e5cdda18d6a027dd66932add5b7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71975" :question/id #uuid "d3537cb5-4e7d-5d82-92f6-bd5301d59474" :question/math-academy-id "q-71975" :question/problem "Find the projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of two sheets $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}=-1$ and the plane $y-2x=2$ onto the $xz$-plane." :question/worked-solution "Since we want to find the projection onto the $xz$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $y.$ First, we solve the equation of the plane for $y$, as follows:\n\n$$\ny-2x=2\\,⟹\\,y=2(x+1)\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $z$ into the equation of the hyperboloid, we obtain: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(2(x+1))^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-(x+1)^{2}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-{x}^{2}-2x-1+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-2x-1+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-2x+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4} & =0 \\\\ -\\frac{{x}^{2}+4x}{2}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by completing the square for the variable $x$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{{x}^{2}+4x}{2}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4} & =0 \\\\ -\\frac{({x}^{2}+4x+4)-4}{2}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4} & =0 \\\\ -\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{2}+2+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{8} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the projection of the intersection is the hyperbola $\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{8}=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71975/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "58427e6a-8e77-5c01-a578-a7dc4b8f8812"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71975"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94953/selection/0e3122eb1e3e126aa10e927535f640abe5db3e233c0b6fb0bdbdf6dcf916a309" :answer/id #uuid "ab79a44d-51c6-5808-9019-adef7aa59c8d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A hyperbola centered at $(-2,4)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94953/selection/bec8408b97e7647b50241fc003ad1f551cf8007b9ba23fd6cf59cc412b666d74" :answer/id #uuid "017bfc71-ea1f-570f-a31d-9b920cfeae2b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A circle centered at $(-1,2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94953/selection/9f8125ae080fc0694d2cc8fb3660c7c5f8a51472192d3627adc6fae023479226" :answer/id #uuid "e44919f7-4605-5a5d-b4ac-cd5ca9cc34ce" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A circle centered at $(-1,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94953/selection/1e75d69e13dee559975ee7b08886eee3411cd78a39bea0c40b56556df16ad9c5" :answer/id #uuid "dc285ebb-d430-5c6a-86d3-7d268958185e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A parabola centered at $(1,-1)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94953/selection/20e011cf5bead7c06f82d07cfa73c3a89338f41ecbd412631a56a671d05c2580" :answer/id #uuid "ff222772-c089-5f01-bda0-9446dfede65b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A hyperbola centered at $(-1,2)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94953/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a8bfbc1a-ac48-5de4-ade4-c564b5b79131" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-94953/selection/bec8408b97e7647b50241fc003ad1f551cf8007b9ba23fd6cf59cc412b666d74" :answer-field/choices ["q-94953/selection/0e3122eb1e3e126aa10e927535f640abe5db3e233c0b6fb0bdbdf6dcf916a309" "q-94953/selection/bec8408b97e7647b50241fc003ad1f551cf8007b9ba23fd6cf59cc412b666d74" "q-94953/selection/9f8125ae080fc0694d2cc8fb3660c7c5f8a51472192d3627adc6fae023479226" "q-94953/selection/1e75d69e13dee559975ee7b08886eee3411cd78a39bea0c40b56556df16ad9c5" "q-94953/selection/20e011cf5bead7c06f82d07cfa73c3a89338f41ecbd412631a56a671d05c2580"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-94953" :question/id #uuid "24927780-1127-5b0b-972c-d7188aac3c99" :question/math-academy-id "q-94953" :question/problem "Which of the following best describes the projection of the intersection between the elliptic cone $\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=(z-2)^{2}$ and the plane $2z-y-6=0$ onto the $xy$-plane?" :question/worked-solution "Since we want to find the projection onto the $xy$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $z.$ First, we solve the equation of the plane for $z,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n2z-y-6=0\\,⟹\\,z=\\frac{y}{2}+3\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $z$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & ={(\\frac{y}{2}+3-2)}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & ={(\\frac{y}{2}+1)}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+y+1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-y & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}-4y+4}{4}-1 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4} & =2 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the equation of a circle of radius $2\\sqrt{2}$ centered at $(-1,2)$ in the $xy$-plane." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94953/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "58427e6a-8e77-5c01-a578-a7dc4b8f8812"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94953"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5264"] :question/problem "Find the point(s) of the intersection of the ellipsoid $\\dfrac{x^2}{24} + \\dfrac{y^2}{24} +\\dfrac{z^2}{6} = 1$ and the line \n${\\begin{aligned}x=4t \\\\ y=8t, \\\\ z=2t\\end{aligned}$ \nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting the expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ from the parametric equation of the line into the equation of the ellipsoid, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{24}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{24}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{6} & =1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+4{z}^{2} & =24 \\\\ (4t)^{2}+(8t)^{2}+4(2t)^{2} & =24 \\\\ 16{t}^{2}+64{t}^{2}+16{t}^{2} & =24 \\\\ 96{t}^{2} & =24 \\\\ {t}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solution $t = \\pm \\dfrac{1}{2}.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=-\\dfrac 1 2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=4(-\\frac{1}{2})=-2 \\\\ y=8(-\\frac{1}{2})=-4 \\\\ z=2(-\\frac{1}{2})=-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $\\left(-2,-4,-1\\right).$\n\n- For $t=\\dfrac 1 2,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=4(\\frac{1}{2})=2 \\\\ y=8(\\frac{1}{2})=4 \\\\ z=2(\\frac{1}{2})=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $\\left(2,4,1\\right).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(-2,-4,-1)$ and $(2,4,1).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12558"] :question/problem "Find the points of the intersection of the elliptic cone $x^2 + y^2=z^2$ and the line $x +1=y-1 =\\dfrac{z}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we write the equation of our line in the parametric form:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083596/assets/41e6a96cc57d9ce57d5a7bec35586175d9217f92e4dc2bab106db641db9f24ea.png)\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\nSubstituting the above expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={z}^{2} \\\\ (t-1)^{2}+(t+1)^{2} & =(2t)^{2} \\\\ {t}^{2}-2t+1+{t}^{2}+2t+1 & =4{t}^{2} \\\\ 2{t}^{2}+2 & =4{t}^{2} \\\\ 2 & =2{t}^{2} \\\\ {t}^{2} & =1 \\\\ t & =\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=-1,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1-1=-2 \\\\ y=-1+1=0 \\\\ z=2(-1)=-2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $\\left(-2,0,-2\\right).$\n\n- For $t=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1-1=0 \\\\ y=1+1=2 \\\\ z=2(1)=2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $\\left(0,2,2\\right).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(-2,0,-2)$ and $(0,2,2).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5618"] :question/worked-solution "Since we want to find the projection onto the $yz$-plane, we need to eliminate the variable $x.$ First, we solve for $x$ in the equation of the plane, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-z=3\\,⟹\\,x=z+3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the expression for $x$ into the equation of the ellipsoid, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{((z+3)+1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(z+4)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{z}^{2}+8z+16}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{2{z}^{2}+8z+16}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}+4z+8}{8} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, by completing the square for the variable $z,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{z}^{2}+4z+8}{8} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{({z}^{2}+4z+4)+4}{8} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(z+2)^{2}+4}{8} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(z+2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{1}{2} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(z+2)^{2}}{8} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}+\\frac{(z+2)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the projection of the intersection is the ellipse $\\dfrac{y^2}{2}+\\dfrac{(z+2)^2}{4} = 1.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
